---
title: Mixed Seafood with Piperade in Scallop Shells
description: Delicate mixed seafood  with cheese served in scallop shells
source: The Novelli Academy ("Beside the Seaside" Course, 20th April 2018)
author: Jean-Christophe Novelli
servings: 4
course: Starter
locale: en_GB
difficulty: Medium
cuisine: French
prep time: 40m
cook time: 20m
tags:
- french
- starter
- seafood
- savoury
---

= Piperade =

Place the @yellow pepper{1}(chopped into small cubes), @courgettes{2}(cut in half then into slices), @aubergine{1}, @cherry tomatoes{300%g}(cut in half), and @onions{2}(chopped) in a large bowl. Add some @honey{squeeze}, 4 of the @garlic{8%cloves}(cracked), half of the @thyme, @spices to taste{}(cumin seeds, coriander seeds, fennel seed, smoked paprika, chilli powder, star anise, cardamom pods, nutmeg), @bay leaf{1}, @salt and @pepper, @olive oil{2%tsp}, @lemon juice{2%tbsp}, @vegetable stock or water{}, and mix well. Cover and leave to infuse for at least ~{30%minutes}.

Heat a large pan and add the vegetables. Cook until slightly coloured and the tomatoes become soft.

Add the @olives{handful}, @anchovy fillets{4}, @mixed herbs{small bunch}(marjoram, thyme, tarragon, parsley), and the rest of the garlic and thyme. Cover and leave the piperade to infuse.

= Fish and Scallop Shells =

In a separate hot pan, sear the @mixed fish fillets, skin left on{300%g} with a little @black pepper{}(ground).

Place some of the piperade in the bottom of the @scallop shells{4}, top with some of the fish and some of the @buffalo mozzarella, or a soft goats cheese like Capricorn{1%large}.

Roll the @puff pastry{200%g} into a long thin strip (needs to be long enough to go round the scallop shell). Place a scallop shell on top of the filled one and with the puff pastry seal the two shells together. Brush the pastry with some @egg{1} wash, decorate with some thyme and dust with a little @flour. Cook in a very hot oven for 3 to ~{4%minutes}, serve immediately.